### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or JetBrains HTTP client).
### Run them top to bottom; variables are captured from previous responses.

@base = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### Health (public)
GET {{base}}/health

### Register
# @name register
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "name": "Ada Lovelace", "password": "Password123!" }

###
@access = {{register.response.body.accessToken}}
@refresh = {{register.response.body.refreshToken}}

### Who am I
GET {{base}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### Create a project
# @name project
POST {{base}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Portfolio", "description": "MVPs for interviews" }

###
@projectId = {{project.response.body.id}}

### Create a task
POST {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Write README", "priority": "high", "dueDate": "2026-12-01T00:00:00.000Z" }

### List tasks (filter + sort + paginate)
GET {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/tasks?priority=high&sort=-createdAt&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### Rotate tokens
# @name refreshed
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### Logout
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshed.response.body.accessToken}}
